# Party banter while exploring Vallaki. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only while its
# condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_smiles
if flag.vallaki_arrived and not flag.festival_over
interject tag:blunt: Look at the smiles on this street. Every one of them put on by order. Not one of them meant.
interject tag:cheerful: I mean mine.
if tag:cheerful
interject class:wizard: Yours is the one that worries them most.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_morale
if flag.baron_met and not flag.festival_over and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:thistle: He locks folk up for frowning? I frown at everything! Big, they'll have me in a cell by supper.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Fear not. I'll do your smiling for you. I've got plenty spare.
interject tag:pious: Joy isn't a wall. It's a window. You can't board it up and still call it one.
endif
-> END

~ banter_saint
if flag.bones_theft_known and not flag.bones_returned and name:kip_smudgewick and class:cleric
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Who steals a saint? Who would you even sell one to? I sold jam to a bishop once, and he haggled.
interject class:cleric: Someone who wants a church to be just a room. Which tells you who.
endif
-> END

~ banter_crates
if flag.henrik_confessed and not flag.coffin_spawn_destroyed and not flag.church_siege_survived
interject class:wizard: Vampire spawn rest by day in the earth they were buried in, or near enough. Inert. Defenceless, the treatises say.
interject tag:blunt: The treatises weren't standing in the storeroom. We go at noon, all together, and we don't open a crate alone.
endif
-> END

~ banter_book_club
if flag.lady_wachter_met and not flag.festival_over and name:wren_featherfoot and name:thistle
interject name:wren_featherfoot: A book club with no books. I knew clubs like that back home. They were always worshipping something. Usually gin.
interject name:thistle: She looked us over like Grandda looks at a hog before market. Not liking. Weighing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_letter
if flag.wachter_evidence and flag.death_house_read_strahd_letter and name:ratatoille and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:ratatoille: The hand in Lady Wachter's letter matches the one under the Durst house. Same loops, same patience. He writes to everybody.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'll take your word for it. My eyes are tired. But a man who writes to everybody wants something from everybody.
interject tag:blunt: He writes to his tools.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pledge_baron
if flag.vallaki_pledge == "baron" and not flag.festival_begun
interject class:cleric: We've sworn ourselves to a man who jails widows for laughing. Someone should say that out loud.
if tag:loyal
interject tag:loyal: Fair. But the other one writes to the castle.
interject class:cleric: That's why I'm still here. It isn't why I'm comfortable.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_pledge_wachter
if flag.vallaki_pledge == "wachter" and not flag.festival_begun and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: She keeps a shrine to the devil of that castle under her own floor, and we have taken her coin. I want that said aloud.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Said. Only, we did shake on it. A bargain's a bargain, even a bad one. Especially a bad one.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then we keep our word, Kip, and we watch her hands while we do.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pledge_town
if flag.vallaki_pledge == "town" and not flag.festival_begun
interject tag:curious: So we're siding with the priest, the innkeeper, and everyone who isn't in charge?
interject tag:blunt: Biggest side in any town. Usually the one that loses.
interject tag:pious: Usually. Not always. Every saint started out on the losing side.
endif
-> END

~ banter_rictavio
if flag.rictavio_unmasked and name:ratatoille and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:ratatoille: Rudolph van Richten, in a feathered hat, on a chair. I have read every word he ever published, twice, and I yawned at him.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Loudly. Twice. I was proud of you.
interject name:ratatoille: It was a very well-informed yawn. Mon dieu. I yawned at Van Richten.
endif
-> END

~ banter_secret
if flag.rictavio_secret_kept
interject tag:curious: We're keeping a vampire hunter's secret, in a valley where the vampire reads everyone's letters.
interject tag:blunt: Then nobody writes it down.
endif
-> END

~ banter_victor
if flag.victor_met and not flag.victor_vanished
interject class:wizard: The boy is genuinely gifted. His circle is the finest piece of work I've seen in this valley, and it is a beautifully drawn door into nothing.
if tag:blunt
interject tag:blunt: Two maids walked through it.
interject class:wizard: Yes. I know. That's the part I can't get past either.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_vanished
if flag.victor_vanished
interject class:wizard: A flash in the attic window. That was the circle. He stepped into it the day his father fell.
interject class:cleric: Sixteen years old. We could have broken that circle with our boots.
endif
-> END

~ banter_arabelle
if flag.arabelle_rescued
interject tag:cheerful: She said one of us is going to lie to the man in the castle, and he's going to like it.
interject tag:blunt: Then nobody lie to him.
interject tag:cheerful: I don't think it's that kind of prophecy.
endif
-> END

~ banter_arrigal
if flag.arrigal_suspected and guest:ireena
interject tag:loyal: The Vistani brother. Arrigal. If he comes near her again, I want to know before she does.
interject tag:curious: He had a saddled horse by his wagon. Night and day. Who keeps a saddled horse for nothing?
endif
-> END

~ banter_vistani
if flag.vistani_friends
interject tag:curious: Every Vistani wagon in Barovia is our wagon now. Do you think that includes the cooking?
if tag:curious
interject class:cleric: It includes the gratitude of a father. That's worth more than stew, and harder to come by.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_ravens
if flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met
interject tag:curious: There's a raven on the roof again. It's the same one. I'm sure it's the same one.
interject tag:blunt: Then it's on our side. Let it watch.
endif
-> END

~ banter_wine
if flag.wizard_of_wines_hook and not flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met
interject tag:curious: No wine coming from the vineyard, no word from the vintner. In Barovia, that's not a supply problem. That's a story nobody's finished telling.
endif
-> END

~ banter_izek_truth
if flag.izek_told_truth
interject class:cleric: He walked out of the square like a man going to bury someone. I suppose he was. Himself, the one he'd been.
interject tag:blunt: Better than burying anyone else.
endif
-> END

~ banter_sanctuary
if flag.ireena_sanctuary == "st_andrals"
interject tag:pious: Holy ground, a good priest, a brother on the door. It's the best we could do for her. I hope it's the best anyone could.
interject tag:blunt: It's walls. She's lived behind walls before. It's what's outside them that worries me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_after_baron
if flag.vallaki_backed == "baron"
interject tag:cheerful: We're Festival Marshals. For life. Every week.
interject tag:blunt: Then we leave town before Thursday.
endif
-> END

~ banter_after_wachter
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
interject class:cleric: She thanked us. In his name. I can still hear it.
if tag:loyal
interject tag:loyal: We kept our word. That has to count for something.
interject class:cleric: It counts. I'm only not sure which side of the ledger.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_after_town
if flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
interject tag:cheerful: A council. Arguing about lamp oil. Out loud. I think that might be the happiest thing I've seen in Barovia.
interject tag:pious: Not a sunrise. But it's facing the right way.
endif
-> END
